# Architecture governance code owners.
#
# This repository has a single maintainer, so a per-path routing table adds no
# information: every path below used to resolve to the same account. One default
# rule keeps the file honest and removes the maintenance cost of re-listing paths
# whenever a governance file moves.
#
# CODEOWNERS only blocks a merge when the protected ruleset enables
# "Require review from Code Owners". Enabling that with a single owner would make
# every PR author-approved-but-unreviewable, so the ruleset stays without it until
# a second reviewer with write access exists.
#
# The paths that actually need care (persisted formats, migration gates, API
# baselines, verification wiring) are named in ARCHITECTURE_GOVERNANCE.md and are
# enforced by gates, not by a routing table: centralized gate wiring is checked by
# `scripts/test/test_ci_coverage.py`, not by a reviewer ping.

